    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s MOR1137 vector drawing and snapped to exact values in small-star-radius units. Four radii and two unit-square diagonals set the cell half-side. The construction shares the unit-star opening with the Meknes and Rabat reconstructions, then adds lines through the guide squares’ corners to make the bands and the small central cross. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. The finished tile edges follow the plain drawing. The opening squares are guides; the cross at O is picked out from them at the ink stage. The palette is illustrative; no photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-26"
  },
